         when={'panel': ('none',), 'ssl': ('own',)}, source='setup doc/lt/09-aplinkos.md:47'),
    Step('env/{env}.env.example in the env repo', 'repo',
         'Address, ports, limits and IP lists – the env repo\'s `env/{env}.env.example`. Do not write `DEPLOY_*`, `APP_UID` or '
         '`APP_GID`: bin/add-project writes them to `target.{env}.env`, and an example with them is refused. Limits are required; '
         'for a server with one project setup suggests ~30 % of the RAM for PHP and ~45 % for the database (split them if the '
         'server is shared). They are ceilings, not reservations: an idle environment takes only the MySQL buffer pool (setup – '
